WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.200
-It's so good to see you.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:03.834
We've had so many fun things
throughout the years,

00:00:03.834 --> 00:00:05.667
but to see you in person,
this means a lot.

00:00:05.667 --> 00:00:08.300
So thanks for coming to
New York and coming on the show.

00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:09.601
We love it.
The audience loves it.

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:10.901
Thank you very much.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.334
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:15.133
We have a lot --
We have a lot to discuss.

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:17.834
-Okay.
-Very excited for you because --

00:00:17.834 --> 00:00:19.868
congratulations --
you just got engaged.

00:00:19.868 --> 00:00:21.601
-Thank you.
-That's a good deal.

00:00:21.601 --> 00:00:25.000
-Thank you.
-I'm happy for you, bud.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.300
I met your beautiful fiancée
backstage.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:30.167
-Yeah.
-And you were telling me that --

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.901
When you introduced me,
you said,

00:00:32.901 --> 00:00:34.767
"This is -- This is Taylor."

00:00:34.767 --> 00:00:35.868
-This is Taylor.
-Yeah.

00:00:35.868 --> 00:00:36.868
-Yeah.

00:00:36.868 --> 00:00:40.701
I'm so narcissistic

00:00:40.701 --> 00:00:43.467
that I wanted to marry somebody

00:00:43.467 --> 00:00:45.701
so I could just call them
Taylor Lautner.

00:00:45.701 --> 00:00:46.934
[ Laughter ]

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.934
-I mean, her name is Taylor.
-Yeah.

00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.767
It gets -- It gets confusing.

00:00:51.767 --> 00:00:53.200
I can only imagine
once we're married

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.901
and we have the same both names.

00:00:55.901 --> 00:00:58.901
But, yeah, we try --

00:00:58.901 --> 00:01:02.200
Her family and friends
call her "Tay," me "Taylor."

00:01:02.200 --> 00:01:04.701
Or they literally just call us
"girl Tay," "boy Tay."

00:01:04.701 --> 00:01:06.167
-Oh, my God.

00:01:06.167 --> 00:01:09.934
I have a photo of you
capturing your proposal.

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:11.501
You're a romantic, buddy.

00:01:11.501 --> 00:01:13.534
You are a romantic guy.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.801
Look at this.
Get ready to swoon over this.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:18.534
[ Audience aws ]
Oh, my goodness.

00:01:18.534 --> 00:01:20.834
-Yeah, I mean,
it's right in our kitchen.

00:01:20.834 --> 00:01:22.534
Like, the fireplace
is right next to our kitchen.

00:01:22.534 --> 00:01:24.734
And this is what I love
about my fiancée

00:01:24.734 --> 00:01:27.567
is she's like,
"I don't want anything special.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:30.033
Like, I just, like, one night
when we're having dinner."

00:01:30.033 --> 00:01:31.834
I love to cook.
She's like, "After you cook,

00:01:31.834 --> 00:01:34.634
we're having a glass of wine,
just do it in the kitchen.

00:01:34.634 --> 00:01:35.834
Like, super simple."

00:01:35.834 --> 00:01:37.000
So, I did it in the kitchen,

00:01:37.000 --> 00:01:38.534
but I did it, like,
big in the kitchen.

00:01:38.534 --> 00:01:40.534
-I mean, candles everywhere,
rose petals.

00:01:40.534 --> 00:01:42.133
-I added a thing or two.

00:01:42.133 --> 00:01:43.434
-A thing or two.

00:01:43.434 --> 00:01:45.934
Oh, my gosh, that's
the most romantic thing ever.

00:01:45.934 --> 00:01:47.701
And you got on one knee.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:50.100
I mean,
she must have freaked out

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:51.801
when she walked in the kitchen.
-She did.

00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:54.434
And she's not really a crier,

00:01:54.434 --> 00:01:58.634
but she was weeping so hard,
she couldn't even walk.

00:01:58.634 --> 00:01:59.801
-Oh, my gosh.

00:01:59.801 --> 00:02:02.167
-And I was on my mark, you know,

00:02:02.167 --> 00:02:03.767
because I wanted
the photos and stuff.

00:02:03.767 --> 00:02:05.467
And I was like,
"Do I have to get off my mark?"

00:02:05.467 --> 00:02:07.367
-Yeah, exactly --
"You got to come closer to me."

00:02:07.367 --> 00:02:10.667
-She would take two steps and,
like, crumble to the ground.

00:02:10.667 --> 00:02:12.634
So I was like, "Crap,
I got to step off the mark."

00:02:12.634 --> 00:02:15.334
And I went and I grabbed her.
And I grabbed her hands.

00:02:15.334 --> 00:02:16.534
I was like, "Babe,

00:02:16.534 --> 00:02:18.100
I have a couple things
I need to say to you.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:20.167
Like, you think you can
come over here with me?"

00:02:20.167 --> 00:02:21.501
[ Laughter ]

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:23.267
-"Because I got this thing
planned out.

00:02:23.267 --> 00:02:25.033
There's like 300 candles here."

00:02:25.033 --> 00:02:26.834
I mean, "Yeah,
and I got things I worked on."

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:29.000
-We only can do this once.
-Once, exactly.

00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:30.501
Have you guys started
planning the wedding yet?

00:02:30.501 --> 00:02:32.200
-We haven't.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.601
We're just, like, so excited
about this stage.

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.167
We're just, like,
soaking it all in.

00:02:36.167 --> 00:02:37.400
-Just in love.

00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.000
When you guys see them,
just you can feel it.

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:41.434
How did you guys meet?

00:02:41.434 --> 00:02:44.067
-My sister introduced us, yeah.

00:02:44.067 --> 00:02:46.300
My little sister.
It's just me and her.

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.701
She's five or six years
younger than me.

00:02:48.701 --> 00:02:51.567
And she met Tay,
and she called me immediately

00:02:51.567 --> 00:02:53.467
and said, "I just met
your future wife.

00:02:53.467 --> 00:02:54.968
You need to meet her."

00:02:54.968 --> 00:02:58.033
So she was like, "You need
to plan a game night."

00:02:58.033 --> 00:02:59.701
I throw a lot of game nights
at the house.

00:02:59.701 --> 00:03:02.400
-Whoo!
-Whoo! All my game-night people.

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:04.667
-Yes. Yeah.
Big following.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.400
The game-night gang.
Yeah, of course.

00:03:06.400 --> 00:03:07.901
-Game-night people
are good people.

00:03:07.901 --> 00:03:09.968
-Of course they are, yeah.

00:03:09.968 --> 00:03:11.968
-And she was like, "Invite me

00:03:11.968 --> 00:03:13.701
and, you know,
a few of my friends,

00:03:13.701 --> 00:03:15.667
and, you know,
Tay will just be one of them.

00:03:15.667 --> 00:03:17.067
It'll be organic."

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.667
And we did that,
and the rest is history.

00:03:19.667 --> 00:03:24.200
-You know when my sister met
my wife now of 14 years, Nancy,

00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.300
she was a producer
on this movie I did.

00:03:26.300 --> 00:03:28.067
And she was there,
and my sister goes,

00:03:28.067 --> 00:03:30.467
"Oh, you're going to marry her."

00:03:30.467 --> 00:03:32.801
And I go,
"No, she's my producer.

00:03:32.801 --> 00:03:34.100
Like, what's going on?"
-She's your producer.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:37.033
Yeah, like, why?
She's like, "No, I can feel it."

00:03:37.033 --> 00:03:38.300
-Wow.
-And I was like --

00:03:38.300 --> 00:03:39.968
So sisters can call it.
-Sisters know best.

00:03:39.968 --> 00:03:42.133
-Yeah, sisters know best.
Congratulations, buddy.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:43.200
-Thank you.

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:45.434
-I want to talk about
"Home Team."

00:03:45.434 --> 00:03:46.801
It's based on the true story

00:03:46.801 --> 00:03:50.334
about New Orleans Saints coach
Sean Payton.

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:52.767
And you're actually friends --

00:03:52.767 --> 00:03:54.100
you're friends with
Sean Payton, right?

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:56.133
-Yeah, yeah.
-How did you get to know him?

00:03:56.133 --> 00:03:59.033
-I met Sean when I was --

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:02.133
I was actually filming the last
two "Twilight" movies in --

00:04:02.133 --> 00:04:05.601
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:05.601 --> 00:04:07.501
I was filming them --

00:04:07.501 --> 00:04:10.334
-You had to know that was
going to get applause.

00:04:10.334 --> 00:04:11.601
I was ready to clap.

00:04:11.601 --> 00:04:13.400
Once you said it,
I was like, "Yeah!

00:04:13.400 --> 00:04:15.367
He said 'Twilight.'
He said 'Twilight.'"

00:04:15.367 --> 00:04:17.167
[ Laughs ]

00:04:17.167 --> 00:04:18.367
He said it. He said it.
Oh, my God.

00:04:18.367 --> 00:04:20.334
-I'm sorry. I'm sorry.
I won't say it again.

00:04:20.334 --> 00:04:22.133
-No, of course.
No, no problem.

00:04:22.133 --> 00:04:23.367
Say whatever you want.

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:25.167
-I was filming them
in Baton Rouge,

00:04:25.167 --> 00:04:29.334
and Sean got ahold of me
and invited me to a home game.

00:04:29.334 --> 00:04:30.434
And I was like, "What?"

00:04:30.434 --> 00:04:32.367
And I show up to the stadium,

00:04:32.367 --> 00:04:35.033
and he's literally there
to open my car door.

00:04:35.033 --> 00:04:36.234
And he's like,
"Nice to meet you, Taylor.

00:04:36.234 --> 00:04:37.934
I'm Sean Payton."
I'm like, "I know."

00:04:37.934 --> 00:04:40.000
And I'm also
looking at my watch.

00:04:40.000 --> 00:04:42.834
And I'm like, "I mean, like,
the game starts in an hour.

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:44.667
Like, don't you have
better things to be doing?"

00:04:44.667 --> 00:04:46.934
He's like, "You want me to
give you a tour of the stadium?

00:04:46.934 --> 00:04:48.767
Like, what do you want to see,
the locker room?"

00:04:48.767 --> 00:04:49.901
-I heard he's just the best.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.100
-He's the coolest dude ever.

00:04:51.100 --> 00:04:53.701
So he literally
gave me my own headphones,

00:04:53.701 --> 00:04:55.734
put me on the sideline
for the game.

00:04:55.734 --> 00:04:57.501
He was like,
"Don't press this button

00:04:57.501 --> 00:04:58.834
or you'll be talking
to Drew Brees."

00:04:58.834 --> 00:05:01.400
I was like, "Okay, I promise."
-Oh, my gosh.

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:02.400
That's wild.

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:04.434
-And that started
our friendship.

00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:07.267
And then cut to like five,
six years later,

00:05:07.267 --> 00:05:10.267
I was filming a movie
in Santa Fe, and he called me.

00:05:10.267 --> 00:05:12.234
And he was like, "Hey, Taylor,
I'm doing, you know,

00:05:12.234 --> 00:05:14.801
me and my daughter's
father/daughter trip this year.

00:05:14.801 --> 00:05:16.200
I'd love to visit you."

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:18.067
I was like, "Come to Santa Fe.
Like, I'm filming a movie.

00:05:18.067 --> 00:05:19.868
Come to set."
So they did.

00:05:19.868 --> 00:05:22.133
And it was there that Meghan,
his daughter,

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:26.367
met a buddy of mine, Sandler's
brother-in-law, Chris Titone,

00:05:26.367 --> 00:05:29.167
and ever since then,
they've been together.

00:05:29.167 --> 00:05:31.968
And Chris wrote this movie
"Home Team" about Meghan's dad.

00:05:31.968 --> 00:05:33.100
-What?

00:05:33.100 --> 00:05:34.834
-Yeah, so it's a crazy
full-circle story.

00:05:34.834 --> 00:05:36.801
-That's crazy full-circle story.
That's awesome.

00:05:36.801 --> 00:05:38.968
-Yeah.
-It's super funny.

00:05:38.968 --> 00:05:41.167
It's got Kevin James.
It's got you.

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:44.467
And, you know, I saw Schneider,
who's super funny.

00:05:44.467 --> 00:05:46.000
Can we set up
what the movie is about?

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:48.167
-Yeah, yeah,
so it's about Sean Payton,

00:05:48.167 --> 00:05:49.734
head coach of
the New Orleans Saints.

00:05:49.734 --> 00:05:53.000
And the year after
they won the Super Bowl,

00:05:53.000 --> 00:05:57.334
he was suspended for a year
from Bountygate.

00:05:57.334 --> 00:06:00.334
And it's about what he did
during that year off.

00:06:00.334 --> 00:06:04.200
And he ended up moving back
to his small hometown in Texas

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:07.667
and helped coach his 12-year-old
son's Pee Wee football team

00:06:07.667 --> 00:06:10.133
and took them to
the state championship game.

00:06:10.133 --> 00:06:13.234
-Yeah. It's so --
It's heartwarming.

00:06:13.234 --> 00:06:14.634
It's for the whole family.
-All a true story. It's crazy.

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.801
-It's a true story.
It's funny.

00:06:16.801 --> 00:06:18.334
We were talking backstage.

00:06:18.334 --> 00:06:21.267
It's kind of like "Bad News
Bears" but for football.

00:06:21.267 --> 00:06:22.868
-Yeah.
-Yeah. It's great.

00:06:22.868 --> 00:06:23.968
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:06:23.968 --> 00:06:25.567
Here's Taylor Lautner
in "Home Team."

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:26.801
Take a look.

00:06:26.801 --> 00:06:29.000
-Look, our season hasn't
got off to the best start.

00:06:29.000 --> 00:06:31.167
-What are you talking about?
We scored a touchdown.

00:06:31.167 --> 00:06:32.834
-We scored a touchdown.

00:06:32.834 --> 00:06:34.367
We didn't get shut down.

00:06:34.367 --> 00:06:35.934
We scored a touchdown.

00:06:35.934 --> 00:06:37.834
-Alright, alright.
True.

00:06:37.834 --> 00:06:40.033
But we did still lose 38-6.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:42.467
-Wow, killing the vibe, Coach.

00:06:42.467 --> 00:06:45.601
-Look, I know each of y'all
are doing your best, okay?

00:06:45.601 --> 00:06:48.734
We just need something to pull
it all together, a new voice.

00:06:48.734 --> 00:06:51.133
-Is Mr. Payton going to be
our new coach?

00:06:51.133 --> 00:06:54.667
-Yeah!

00:06:54.667 --> 00:06:58.901
-Coach Payton is going to be
our new offensive coordinator.

00:06:58.901 --> 00:07:00.167
-Oh, okay.

00:07:00.167 --> 00:07:01.634
-How about that?

00:07:01.634 --> 00:07:04.434
-Our defense sucks, too.

00:07:04.434 --> 00:07:05.567
-Thank you.

00:07:05.567 --> 00:07:06.534
[ Laughter ]

00:07:06.534 --> 00:07:08.234
-That's a good line read.

00:07:08.234 --> 00:07:09.901
That's a good read.

00:07:09.901 --> 00:07:11.667
Taylor Lautner, everybody.

00:07:11.667 --> 00:07:13.801
"Home Team" is streaming now
on Netflix.

